# Parallelism soundness Phase 6 (P-23): the worker pool's atexit handler used to
# JOIN every worker, so a task still blocked when the program ends (here: an
# hour-long sleep) kept the process alive for good
# (issues/fixed/worker-pool-atexit-shutdown-joins-workers-blocked-in-a-task.md).
# A pool held in a module global is never dropped, and exit does not wait for
# its workers. The case's timeout is the oracle: a runtime that waited would
# never let the test binary exit, and the case would time out.
stdout_keep_match=1 passed
timeout=120
